/* bsp_stm32h5.c - board support for STM32H5 (STM32H573I-DK for now, own board later).
 *
 * Uses only handles and pin labels generated by STM32CubeMX (docs/CUBEMX_SETUP.md):
 *   GPIO user labels DI_01..DI_22 (inputs) and DO_01..DO_20 (outputs). A channel
 *   whose label is not defined in main.h is simply absent (reads 0, writes ignored),
 *   so the DK can run with whatever pins it has free and the real board fills in
 *   the rest. Pin polarity: define DI_nn_ACTIVE_LOW / DO_nn_ACTIVE_LOW to 1 in
 *   main.h (USER CODE section) for active-low wiring; the default is active high.
 *   hrtc  (RTC, calendar in binary)     hiwdg (IWDG, about 1 s)
 * No pin numbers are assumed here: they belong to the schematic and the .ioc. */
